## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of explainability and governance as essential components of production ML workflows, not just model performance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Clarify for feature attributions and bias detection
- Model Registry and Pipelines for full traceability and lineage
- Lightweight dashboards (QuickSight) for non-technical stakeholders
- Drift detection and automated rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Call SageMaker Clarify for per-inference feature attributions
const explanation = await clarify.explain({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  data: { text: 'This product is amazing!' }
});

// Retrieve bias score
const biasReport = await clarify.getBiasScore({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  dataset: 'production-reviews'
});

// Register model with explanations
await modelRegistry.register({
  modelName: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  explanations: explanation,
  biasScore: biasReport
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience building production ML pipelines in AWS with strict data locality, latency targets, and privacy. Assesses ability to combine PrivateLink, Lake Formation, Feature Store, canary deployment, drift monitoring, and cost governance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker PrivateLink
- Lake Formation data access
- Feature Store
- Endpoint traffic splitting (canary)
- Drift detection & retraining triggers
- DP privacy controls and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example drift score calculation (KS statistic placeholder)
function ksDrift(p, q) {
  let max = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < p.length; i++) {
    max = Math.max(max, Math.abs(p[i] - q[i]));
  }
  return max;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rollback if canary drift triggers fire?
- What metrics and thresholds would you alert on for latency, FP rate, and drift?
